WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.155 --> 00:00:03.560
- [Narrator] Ah vodka, always
a good choice. (jazzy music)

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.393
Strong, smooth, delightfully clear.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:12.470
Vodka is usually made from
potatoes, grapes, or wheat.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.800
One man is doing things differently.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.750
He's making vodka from (sheep calling).

00:00:17.674 --> 00:00:20.070
Yes, you heard that right.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:21.053
Sheep.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.740
(upbeat music)

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.320
- We are in Birchs Bay,
in Tasmania, Australia.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:35.760
Sixteen years ago my family and I built

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.600
our sheep cheesery from scratch.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.680
You know, I was getting
tired of just doing

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.620
the sort of cheese things.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:45.540
And so I came up with
the idea of distilling.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:46.580
- [Narrator] But how?

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:47.463
By using whey.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:52.620
- So whey is essentially
part of cheesemaking.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.100
And in a lot of cases put
down the drain and wasted.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.923
I have figured out a way to
turn that into a product.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.690
- [Narrator] Making vodka
from whey is quite unusual.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.880
There have been a couple
successful attempts,

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.520
but no one had ever made
a sheep's whey vodka.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.370
Until Ryan came along.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:12.420
It took him about 100 attempts
over the course of a year,

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:13.793
but he got there.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.760
- So, step one: we milk the sheep,

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.390
and then give it to our cheese factory,

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:21.400
who then makes it into a cheese,

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.570
and then the whey is what's leftover.

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:26.030
Step two: I grab that whey-

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:29.020
and then adding enzymes-it
ferments into alcohol.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.570
What essentially creates
alcohol is a basic sugar.

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:34.740
And my basic sugar is lactose.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.980
Step three: I grab that alcohol

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:39.890
and distill it twice
into a finished spirit.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:44.470
And step four: I age the
spirit for four months.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:47.460
Step five: we actually
hand-paint the entire bottle.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:50.160
So we spray the black on,
and then we hand-write,

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:51.920
so that every bottle is unique.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:53.640
Start to finish, from milking the sheep,

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.350
all the way to bottling the product,

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.235
it would take at least five months.

00:01:57.235 --> 00:01:58.440
(peppy music)

00:01:58.440 --> 00:01:59.740
You'll smell a lot of sweetness

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:01.380
coming through from the milk.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:02.300
And then when you drink it,

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.680
it's gonna be really
creamy on the palette.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.200
And almost have a little
milky sort of finish.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.440
One of the biggest awards that we won

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.990
was World's Best Vodka,
which was huge for us.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.260
- [Narrator] And vodka is not the end

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.023
for Ryan's distilling experiments.

00:02:16.023 --> 00:02:18.930
He's also ventured into gin.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.713
And now, to cue us out,
how do you drink it?

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:25.690
- So treat it really
really similar to a whisky.

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:26.653
Just nice and neat.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.773
Even with no ice.

00:02:30.594 --> 00:02:31.544
Yeah, that's great.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:35.790
- That's really smooth.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:37.367
- That's really nice.

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:39.093
- Mm, beautiful.

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:40.820
Very nice spirit.

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:44.691
Could drink this, yes definitely.

00:02:44.691 --> 00:02:46.858
Beautiful to the palette.

